 knowledge variant of the sumcheck protocol [LFKN92] in the IPCP model.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBits Under ZK-LLM: Evaluating Zero-Knowledge-Friendly Quantization for Verifiable Private LLM Inference (https://arxiv.org/html/2609.36437v1)\nciteturn3view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2609.36437v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 565\nL0: ##### Report GitHub Issue\nL1: \nL2: [Button: ×]\nL3: \nL4: Title: [Input: Enter title]\nL5: \nL6: Content selection saved. Describe the issue below:\nL7: \nL8: Description:\nL9: \nL10: [Button: Submit without GitHub] [Button: Submit in GitHub]\nL11: \nL12: 【0†Back to arXiv】\nL13: \nL14: 【1†Why HTML?†info.arxiv.org】 【2†Report Issue】 【3†Back to Abstract】 【4†Download PDF】\nL15:   1. 【5†Abstract】\nL16:   2. 【6†1 Introduction】\nL17:   3. 【7†2 Background and Related Work】\nL18:     1. 【8†Zero-Knowledge Proofs.】\nL19:     2. 【9†Post-Training Quantization.】\nL20:     3. 【10†Quantization in ZK-ML.】\nL21:   4. 【11†3 ZK-friendly Quantization】\nL22:     1. 【12†ZK efficiency.】\nL23:     2. 【13†Fidelity.】\nL24:   5. 【14†4 Methods】\nL25:     1. 【15†Research Questions.】\nL26:     2. 【16†ZK-aware Quantization Framework.】\nL27:     3. 【17†Scalable Estimation of ZK Proving Cost.】\nL28:     4. 【18†Implementation and experiment setup.】\nL29:   6. 【19†5 Results】\nL30:     1. 【20†5.1 Broad Utility Study】\nL31:       1. 【21†R1. Activations are more sensitive to low precision than weights】\nL32:       2. 【22†R2. A uniform B16 LUT configuration does not reliably preserve utility】\nL33:       3. 【23†R3. RMSNorm inverse-square-root LUTs are a recurring utility bottleneck】\nL34:     2. 【24†5.2 End-to-End Proving Costs】\nL35:       1. 【25†5.2.1 Floating-point vs. Quantized proving at Qwen-14B scale】\nL36:       2. 【26†5.2.2 Proving cost does not scale smoothly with quantization】\nL37:         1. 【27†R4. End-to-end proving tim