L146: ##\nL147: \nL148: 【77†[HVZK-WHIR 3/6] HVZK sumcheck with sublinear masks】#1605\nL149: \nL150: 【70†tcoratger】 merged 48 commits into\nL151: \nL152: 【71†Plonky3:main】Plonky3/Plonky3:main from\nL153: \nL154: 【72†camofu:carlo/hv-sumcheck】camofu/Plonky3:carlo/hv-sumcheck Copy head branch name to clipboard\nL155: \nL156: ## Conversation\nL157: \nL158: ###\nL159: \nL160: 【78†Image: @camofu†avatars.githubusercontent.com】 【79†camofu】 commented 【80†May 4, 2026】 •\nL161: \nL162: edited\nL163: \nL164: Loading\nL165: ### Uh oh!\nL166: \nL167: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL168: \nL169: Copy link\nL170: \nL171: Copy Markdown\nL172: \nL173: Closes 【81†#1586】. Part of the HVZK-WHIR effort tracked in 【82†#1590】. Depends on 【83†#1584】 (ZK encoding traits, now in `p3-zk-codes` since 【84†#1601】).\nL174: ## Background\nL175: \nL176: WHIR's sumcheck currently reduces a claim about a `2^k`-interleaved Reed–Solomon codeword to a claim about the base codeword by sending `k` univariate round-polynomials `ĥ_1, …, ĥ_k`. Each `ĥ_j` is a linear function of the secret witness `f`, so it leaks information — fine for non-private WHIR, but incompatible with the HVZK-WHIR effort tracked in 【82†#1590】.\nL177: 【85†Construction 6.3 of eprint 2026/391†eprint.iacr.org】 (\"Zero-Knowledge IOPPs for Constrained Interleaved Codes\", Chiesa–Fenzi–Weissenberg, Feb 2026) shows how to make this sumcheck honest-verifier zero-knowledge with only `Õ(k·λ)` extra field elements — i.e. the zero-knowledge overhead is independent of the witness size, which is what gives the paper its headline `1 + o(1)` overhead property.\nL178: ## Goal\nL179: \nL180: Add an HVZK variant of the WHIR sumcheck in `whir/src/sumcheck/zk.rs` implementing Construction 6.3:\nL1133: ### Uh oh!\nL1134: \nL1135: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL1136: \nL1137: 【70†tcoratger】 enabled auto-merge (squash) 【160†May 14, 2026 13:46】\nL1138: \nL1139: Hide details View details\nL1140: \nL1141: