ociated\nL906:       constants, and `!=` between them dispatches through `PartialEq::ne`,\nL907:       which is not callable in const context on stable Rust (would require\nL908:       the unstable `const_trait_impl` feature).\nL909:     - Re-add the dropped trailing `;` on the inlined `n_claims` binding.\nL910: \nL911:     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nL912: ` 【143†[HVZK-WHIR 3/6] bump bench ELL_ZK from 4 to 37 for soundness-realisti…】 ` [Button: … ]\nL913: \nL914: [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL915: ` 【143†daa1fc1】 `\nL916: \nL917:     …c measurement\nL918: \nL919:     `ELL_ZK = 4` minimises the mask-side work (8-leaf Merkle tree) and lets\nL920:     the ≤ 1.05× HVZK overhead target pass against a toy parameter, not a\nL921:     parameter the soundness analysis would actually pick.\nL922: \nL923:     Theorem 1 of eprint 2026/391 (§2.7) instantiates the mask code as a\nL924:     Reed-Solomon code with message length `O(λ / log log λ)`. For `λ = 100`\nL925:     that puts ℓ_zk at roughly 37, so the bench now measures HVZK overhead\nL926:     against a mask size the real protocol would use.\nL927: \nL928:     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nL929: ` 【144†[HVZK-WHIR 3/6] hoist virtual-claim alpha powers out of the round loop】 ` [Button: … ]\nL930: \nL931: [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL932: ` 【144†508640f】 `\nL933: \nL934:     The round loop rebuilt `alpha.powers().skip(n_claims)` every iteration\nL935:     to pair virtual claims with their `α^i` weights. Continue the existing\nL936:     `alphas` iterator past the concrete-claim collects into a single\nL937:     `virtual_alphas: Vec<EF>` before the loop, then read it by slice from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReleases · ingonyama-zk/icicle · GitHub (https://github.com/ingonyama-zk/icicle/releases)\nciteturn3view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"tu